    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS take great pleasure in introducing no. 255B Cherrywood Lawns to the open market - an ideal family home tucked away to the rear of this charming development. Every conceivable amenity can be found within striking distance; local shops & schools, Corkagh Park, bars & restaurants & Clondalkin village to name but a few. Transport links abound with the M50, N7, N4 and the LUAS all within easy reach.\nBright and spacious internal living space of c. 76 sq m comprises of entrance hallway, open plan kitchen/dining room, lounge, three bedrooms (two double 1 single) and main family bathroom. To the rear is a well maintained garden area and to the front there is off street parking for multiple cars.\nNo. 255B is presented in good condition throughout and offers huge potential for a first time buyer that is looking to lay down roots in an established area. The long list of additional features includes built in storage, dual aspect living space & gas fired central heating.\nA rare gem and certainly one not to let pass you by, Call Ray Cooke Auctioneers to register your interest today.\nFeatures\n- c. 76 sq m\n- BER C3\n- Ideally located at the end of the cul de sac\n- 3bed 2bath Semi Detached\n- Off street parking to front\n- Well presented throughout\n- Laminate flooring\n- Dual aspect living space\n- Gas fired central heating\n- Fitted kitchen with ample storage units and worktop space\n- Prime position within the development with limited passing traffic\n- Within short walking distance of local convenience stores & amenities\n- Within walking distance of Clondalkin Village\n Bus routes conveniently located to the front of the development\n- M50, N7 & N4 motorway found merely minutes by car\n- Viewing highly recommended\nDirections\nFrom Red Cow roundabout proceed along Naas Road. Turn right at Newlands Cross (Maldron Hotel). Continue along the Fonthill Road and after the first mini roundabout turn left onto the Old Nangor Road. Continue straight ahead and at the next roundabout turn left onto cherrywood Crescent. Take a right along Cherrywood Park and then a left will bring you to Cherrywood Lawns where number 225 B will be on your right hand side."
      },
      {
